title: 'M1.11 slice 3: gnomon mod CLI meets the kernel through the home, not a new verb'
summary: No socket verb exists for install/pause/start/uninstall (adding one moves clientApiId), so the CLI stages files under the home mods dir and the daemon StagedCardPickup raises them through the real approval broker, which re-derives every card from the pinned snapshot. Uninstall is a root-class grant card appending a root-signed grant.uninstall row; GRANT_ROW_KINDS is not a clientApiId input.
